Freqtrade (GPL-3.0) and how this project relates to it
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Freqtrade (https://github.com/freqtrade/freqtrade) is licensed under the GNU
General Public License v3.0. This repository does not contain or redistribute
Freqtrade's code. It is used as the unmodified upstream Docker image
(freqtradeorg/freqtrade), pinned in infra/docker-compose.yml.

- Conductor (services/conductor) talks to Freqtrade only over its REST API,
  as a separate program in a separate container.
- These files import Freqtrade's Python modules and run inside the Freqtrade
  container:
    services/freqtrade/user_data/strategies/*.py
    services/research/strategies/*.py
    services/research/src/research_harness/ft_runner.py
  They are this project's own code and are licensed under Apache-2.0. The
  Apache License 2.0 is compatible with GPLv3 (in that direction), so they may
  be combined with Freqtrade. If you distribute a combined work (for example
  a container image that bundles Freqtrade with these files), that
  distribution must comply with the GPL-3.0.

This summary is not legal advice.

